WEBVTT

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.710
Here.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.540
It’s hot chocolate, your favorite.

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:18.070
Where am I?

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.810
Don’t you remember?

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:24.150
We lived in this cottage
when we were young.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:27.960
Oh. I don’t remember.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.420
You used to laugh a lot back then.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:36.580
You talked a lot and
told many jokes.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:40.990
Haruto...

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:44.600
The person who did this to you is...

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:55.830
Am I bothering you?

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.660
Haruto, it’s time to work.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:03.370
Mr. Heartland, Haruto collapsed
because he used too much power.

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:06.330
Haruto shouldn’t use
his power again.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:10.710
Kaito, these are Dr. Faker’s orders.

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:11.990
But…

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:14.380
I hate you.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:18.210
Brother, I hate you because
you don’t think about others.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:19.180
Haruto...

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.400
I don’t mind.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:25.080
If my power helps this world...

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.650
You don’t need to worry about me.

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:29.610
Haruto...

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.840
Fantastic, Haruto!

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:35.060
Dr. Faker will also be happy!

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:40.280
Kaito, if you really
want to heal Haruto,

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:44.450
you should gather all the Numbers
as fast as possible.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.710
Ouch...

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:03.260
There’s an airship
inside the King’s Key?

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:04.310
Yes.

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:06.520
Inside this tiny key?

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.520
That key isn’t from this world.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:15.740
Your father’s key
contains many mysteries.

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:19.350
Does the airship fly?

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:23.790
The airship is built
like a giant puzzle.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:29.810
I need Numbers in order
to solve the puzzle.

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:37.260
When we gather all the
Numbers, that airship will...

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:39.840
Numbers...

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:56.730
Orbital, we’re resuming
the hunt for Numbers.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:00.210
What’s the status, Orbital?

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.210
Orbital 7!

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:04.700
Understood!

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:07.430
Master Kaito!

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:08.330
You...

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:13.080
Did you finish analyzing the
duelists who have Numbers?

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.000
Well, um...

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.310
I despise incompetence.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:20.170
Are you incompetent?

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:22.040
Understood! Understood!

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:24.180
Please don’t turn me into scrap!

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:27.290
Find the original Number.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:28.340
Original?

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.310
Yeah.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:34.360
Dr. Faker said that an envoy
brought the Numbers to this world.

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:39.780
That original envoy must
have possessed someone.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.640
Original...

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:46.950
Then Master Kaito, I discovered
something interesting!

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:50.430
Yuma Tsukumo, the Number
duelist you battled the other day,

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.880
was wearing
this strange pendant.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.960
What’s that?

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.800
It’s not from this world.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.050
What?

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:02.340
That duelist...

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:08.520
Gather information
about him immediately!

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.220
Understood!

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:13.410
Yuma Tsukumo...

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:20.650
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:23.780
They give color to each day Will
and love keep me from losing heart

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.700
Your kindness was harsh I learned
frustration when we clashed

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.450
Freedom begins by
accepting differences

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:30.950
Dance and create the universe

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:38.340
In truth, I was sad until I met you

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:44.920
I lied, thinking it was
easier to be alone

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:51.430
Even though we don’t like
the same books or hobbies

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:55.310
You’re the only one
who agreed with me

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.440
Joy and sadness and anger
and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:00.350
There’s no harmony and
scenario without differences

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:03.610
Everyone is not the same

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:08.530
That’s the reason for living

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:13.790
Even if the sounds are
dissonant at times

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:19.210
That’s why I never give up I believe
my strength will get me through

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:23.150
I travel to the edge of the world

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:26.930
The sights I see with
you are the truth

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:29.760
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.310
They give color to each day Will
and love keep me from losing heart

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:36.390
Your kindness was harsh I learned
frustration when we clashed

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:38.020
Freedom begins by
accepting differences

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:40.520
Dance and create the universe

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:46.490
Oh no!

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:50.880
I forgot that we’re swimming in the pool for P.E. today!

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:55.160
\hThe King’s Key is Stolen! Clash: Kaito vs Shark\h

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:55.160
Number 22:

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:53.550
He’s frantic as usual.

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:55.160
I’m relieved.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:58.160
You’ve come back to school.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:03.340
Did Yuma change your heart?

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:08.510
He has a strange power
that’s like the sun.

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:13.930
Yuma brightens the hearts of
everyone he interacts with.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.480
Don’t you think so?

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:19.190
Who knows.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:22.100
Hey, will Yuma kattobing today?

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:23.180
Who knows?

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:24.550
I look forward to it.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:25.290
I guess.

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:27.140
Stop!

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:28.400
What is it?

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:32.110
You’re not allowed to wear
your pendant during pool time!

00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:33.780
Why?

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:37.500
To summarize, because
it’s dangerous!

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.250
It’s not dangerous!

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.960
I agree.

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:43.920
Yuma, remember the
last time you jumped

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.340
into the pool while
wearing your pendant?

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:49.800
It got stuck into
someone’s head, remember?

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:52.970
Stuck? Who’s head?

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:53.550
Oh no...

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:57.310
My head!

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:03.110
Sheesh, the class representative
sure holds a grudge.

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:10.180
Is Astral really
inside this tiny key?

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:12.740
Well, stay here.

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:21.810
A strange power that’s
like the sun...

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:32.260
I don’t want to be
turned into scrap.

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:36.910
That pendant must hold a secret.

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:44.440
Number Cards are
pieces of my memories.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:47.860
We’ve retrieved 10 cards.

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:56.740
What is this memory?

00:07:57.970 --> 00:08:00.880
It’s no good. I can’t remember.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:03.460
I have to gather more Numbers.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.340
I know it’s here.

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:09.210
I’ll search for it.

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.090
Target confirmed!

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.430
I’m taking it!

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:22.850
Mission complete.

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:25.010
What are you doing?

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:26.150
Well...

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:30.610
Give back the pendant before
I’m turned into scrap!

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:33.320
I don’t know what
you’re talking about.

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:39.490
How dare you!

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:44.890
I’ll force you to give
me back that pendant!

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:49.870
One of us is going to
be turned into scrap!

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:51.600
What is it?

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:54.050
Let’s fight!

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:03.680
Wait!

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:12.430
What? The key is stopping!

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:22.880
The Numbers I set have been removed.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:25.560
The King’s Key has closed?

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:39.510
Hand over the pendant!

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:43.060
That’s enough, Orbital!

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:47.980
How dare you act on your own?

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:48.770
Master Kaito!

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:52.780
Hand over the pendant.

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:56.030
No. It isn’t yours.

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:59.070
I know. It belongs to Yuma Tsukumo.

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:00.740
You know Yuma?

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:04.080
Yeah, because he has Numbers.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.740
Numbers... I see.

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:08.540
Are you the Number Hunter?

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:11.210
So you know who I am.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:12.880
Do you also have a Number?

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:15.590
What if I do?

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:18.200
Then that’s great for me!

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:21.610
I’ll take both your Number
Card and that pendant!

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:22.810
Let’s duel!

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:25.720
Yuma...

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:30.210
It’s time for me to pay my debt.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:34.610
Fine! I’ll take you on!

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:39.660
Duel mode! Photon change!

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:46.440
Duel Disk set!

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:56.760
D-Gazer set!

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:04.220
I’ll hunt your soul!

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:11.430
AR Vision Link complete.

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:13.650
Duel!

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:15.200
This is horrible.

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:16.810
What a mess.

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:18.320
Who did this?

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:21.570
To summarize, I don’t think
a human could’ve done this.

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:24.240
It’s not here!

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.740
The King’s Key is missing!

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:29.210
I’ll go first!

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:32.590
My turn! I draw!

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:37.840
If he’s a Number Hunter,
he must have many Numbers.

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:41.510
But I have a plan to
defeat the Numbers!

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:44.920
I send Big Jaws in my
hand to the graveyard

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:47.970
to activate the Continuous Spell
Shark Lair from my hand!

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:50.430
As long as this card’s effect is active,

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:55.150
monsters with equal or fewer ATK than the monster
I sent to the graveyard can’t attack!

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:58.360
Big Jaws has 1800 ATK.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:03.360
Your monsters with 1800 or fewer
ATK are sealed away!

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:06.370
Next, I summon Shocktopus!

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:14.080
I set one card and end my turn!

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:17.040
Summon your Number!

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:23.550
My turn! I draw!

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:27.010
I activate the spell card
Polymerization from my hand!

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:28.720
Polymerization?

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:32.430
I fuse two Photon
Lizards from my hand!

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:35.400
By sending these specific
monsters to the graveyard,

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:39.230
I can Special Summon a Fusion
Monster from my Extra Deck.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:44.360
Fusion Summon! Appear,
Twin Photon Lizard!

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:49.760
By Fusion Summoning, he can bring out
a powerful monster from the start.

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:53.590
He used Fusion Summon
instead of Xyz Summon.

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:56.830
He knows how to use
different strategies.

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:59.160
Your spell card works
against monsters

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:01.820
with 1800-or-fewer ATK.

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:05.130
That won’t work against me.

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:07.300
Go, Twin Photon Lizard!

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:09.530
Sublime Breath!

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:17.560
Shocktopus’s effect activates!

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:21.090
It equips on to your
monster that destroyed

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:24.650
Shocktopus, and that monster
now has 0 ATK!

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:28.990
And the equipped monster can’t
change battle position!

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:33.950
In other words, your monster remains
on the field with 0 ATK!

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:36.200
I turned the tables!

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:39.460
On the next turn, I’ll
deal you big damage.

00:13:40.350 --> 00:13:42.720
He is unexpectedly skilled.

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:44.840
Your plans won’t come to fruition.

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:45.880
What?

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:49.140
I activate Twin Photon
Lizard’s effect!

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:55.060
When this monster’s Fusion-Material Monsters
are in the graveyard, I can undo the fusion!

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:03.480
He has two Level 3 monsters!
Is it coming?

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:07.200
I overlay two Level
3 Photon Lizards!

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:12.980
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:15.830
Xyz Summon!

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:24.050
Appear, Number 30!

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:27.720
Melt everything with
your abominable power!

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.220
Acid Golem of Destruction!

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:34.740
3000 ATK!

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:37.140
This is his Number!

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:44.400
I’ve hooked an incredible catch.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:47.030
I activate the trap Splash Capture!

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:53.530
When you Xyz Summon, I banish
two Fish-Type monsters

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:58.400
in my graveyard to gain
control of your Xyz Monster.

00:14:58.400 --> 00:15:02.880
I banish Big Jaws and
Shocktopus from my graveyard!

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:05.340
You fell for it, Number Hunter!

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:10.010
My goal was to make you
summon a powerful monster!

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:19.950
Now I gain control of Acid Golem!

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:25.940
I took a powerful Number
with 3000 ATK!

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:28.110
This duel is mine!

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:30.520
Master Kaito, isn’t this bad?

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:32.480
Back off.

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:33.820
Understood.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:37.790
I activate the spell
card Forced Release!

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:45.000
An Xyz Monster’s Overlay Units
are all sent to the graveyard!

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:48.460
I set one card and end my turn!

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:51.930
He got rid of its Overlay Units.

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:54.890
But I still have 3000 ATK!

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:57.410
My turn! I draw!

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:02.610
You’ll now take Acid Golem’s curse!

00:16:02.610 --> 00:16:04.270
Curse?

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:18.800
Acid Golem is a
self-destructive Number.

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:27.170
As a drawback for having 3000 ATK when it’s only Rank 3, it has many curses.

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:29.170
What?

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:37.800
One curse is that if you don’t use an Overlay Unit every time it’s your turn, you take 2000 points of damage.

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:43.440
But Acid Golem still
has its ATK!

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:47.070
Go, Acid Golem!
Attack him directly!

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:47.950
It’s no good.

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:48.610
What?

00:16:48.990 --> 00:16:53.110
Acid Golem can’t attack
unless it has Overlay Units.

00:16:53.890 --> 00:16:55.040
What?

00:16:55.040 --> 00:17:01.540
I knew that you would use a spell card if I summoned a powerful Number.

00:17:01.900 --> 00:17:04.500
I’m the one who fell into a trap.

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:08.940
At this rate, I’ll self-destruct
due to Acid Golem’s effect.

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:12.950
The Number Hunter is
incredibly strong.

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:16.880
Am I going to lose?

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:22.640
Oh yeah.

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:24.480
Yuma...

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:29.400
I set one card and end my turn!

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:32.150
My turn! I draw!

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:35.440
The card I set is Life Regeneration.

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:40.370
If I take effect damage on my
turn, that damage is negated.

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.870
There still must be a way to win.

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:44.580
I’ll never give up!

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:49.380
I activate the spell
card Photon Sublimation!

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:55.540
By banishing two Photon monsters from my graveyard, I can draw two cards!

00:17:55.540 --> 00:17:58.800
I banish two Photon Lizards!

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.760
I draw two cards!

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:04.790
I Special Summon Photon Thrasher!

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:10.520
I can Special Summon Photon Thrasher
when I have no monsters on my field.

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:13.510
Then I Normal Summon Photon Crusher!

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:18.700
Here I go.

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:23.410
I tribute these two
monsters to Special Summon!

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:24.870
Summon what?

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:29.960
This monster can’t
be Normal Summoned.

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:34.460
I have to tribute monsters with 2000-or-more ATK to Special Summon it.

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:42.460
The embodiment of light descends!

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:46.770
What?

00:18:50.240 --> 00:18:53.150
Appear, Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:18:56.950 --> 00:18:59.170
Astral!

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:01.570
What?

00:19:02.610 --> 00:19:04.300
What’s going on?

00:19:05.820 --> 00:19:07.170
Yuma!

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:09.290
What’s that cloud?

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:11.140
Can it be?

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:12.750
Yuma!

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:19.290
Something is happening
in the outside world.

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:21.460
What?

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:25.680
The time has come.

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:29.390
You must attain the power of ZEXAL.

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:33.390
The power that changes
all darkness into light.

00:19:33.390 --> 00:19:35.020
ZEXAL.

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:40.320
What’s that monster?

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.320
This is the end.

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:45.690
Photon Stream of Destruction!

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:52.790
What? You’re attacking a Number?

00:19:58.040 --> 00:19:59.230
No way!

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:01.510
Galaxy-Eyes isn’t a Number.

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:03.470
How can it destroy a Number?

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:12.690
If Acid Golem is attacked when it has no Overlay Units, it’s destroyed.

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:17.360
But your attack was a mistake!

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:21.740
You saved me from
Acid Golem’s curse!

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:26.790
Me, make a mistake?
You’re a romanticist.

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:27.700
What?

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:30.150
The curse isn’t over yet.

00:20:30.150 --> 00:20:36.650
When Acid Golem is destroyed,
its controller takes 2000 points of damage.

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:39.950
What?

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:06.570
I’m sorry, Yuma.

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:08.280
I’ll hunt you.

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:13.160
Along with your soul.

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:26.520
This soul doesn’t have a Number.

00:21:26.520 --> 00:21:28.580
Shark?

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:29.930
Yuma Tsukumo.

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:32.430
You’re Kaito!

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:36.750
Shark...

00:21:39.280 --> 00:21:41.070
What did you do to him?

00:21:41.430 --> 00:21:45.530
Master Kaito, your Photon
Mode burden is at 85%.

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:47.910
Dueling more will be—

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:49.010
I know.

00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:50.990
That’s the King’s Key!

00:22:05.430 --> 00:22:08.970
Astral!

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:15.790
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:15.790 --> 00:22:17.910
This week’s quiz:

00:22:17.910 --> 00:22:21.760
Which monster can you Xyz Summon
with two Level 4 monsters?

00:22:21.760 --> 00:22:24.860
Utopia or Leviathan Dragon?

00:22:30.630 --> 00:22:35.230
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:35.230 --> 00:22:39.920
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:50.330 --> 00:22:54.830
Anyway, tests are hard Language,
math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.830 --> 00:22:59.520
Average scores in science and social
studies I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.970 --> 00:23:02.520
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:04.820
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.820 --> 00:23:07.240
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.690 --> 00:23:08.860
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:09.350 --> 00:23:13.990
Let’s say I wrote the correct
answers on that sheet

00:23:13.990 --> 00:23:18.120
Will that change the future a
year or a decade from now?

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:23.930
The world I drew at
the edge of dreams

00:23:23.930 --> 00:23:28.760
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.760 --> 00:23:33.600
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:37.500
Nothing is correct!

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:43.020
Kaito took Shark’s soul!

00:23:43.020 --> 00:23:45.320
And he also took the King’s
Key with Astral inside!

00:23:45.890 --> 00:23:48.940
I have to find Kaito
in order to save them!

00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:52.100
It’s finally time for
us to battle, Kaito!

00:23:52.100 --> 00:23:53.570
Yuma, your deck!

00:23:53.570 --> 00:23:57.950
I can sense that Astral is battling!

00:23:57.950 --> 00:24:03.250
I won’t give up because my dear
friend taught me about kattobing.

00:24:03.250 --> 00:24:09.840
\h\hDuel of Destiny! Astral vs Kaito\h\h

00:24:03.250 --> 00:24:08.000
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“Duel of Destiny! Astral vs Kaito”

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:09.950
I’m kattobing!

00:24:11.720 --> 00:24:15.120
The answer is... Utopia!

00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:19.870
You can Xyz Summon Utopia by
using two Level 4 monsters.

00:24:19.870 --> 00:24:24.410
There are many other Xyz
Monsters, so try them out!
